.TH CPPIC 1 "2026-09-18" "cppic 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cppic \- C++ to C transpiler for PIC18 microcontrollers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cppic
[\fI--lex\fR | \fI--dump\fR | \fI--emit\fR] [\fI-I dir\fR]
\fIfile.cpp\fR [\fImore.cpp\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cppic
compiles the C++ subset used in Arduino sketches (object-oriented C++)
into plain C suitable for SDCC and 8-bit PIC18 microcontrollers.
The generated C is self-contained and includes the PIC18 runtime.
.PP
Input files are preprocessed (a C-preprocessor subset: #include, #define,
#ifdef/#if/#elif/#else/#endif, #error) and linked into one translation
unit, so sketches split across several files are supported.
.PP
The Arduino-style \fBString\fR type is supported (concatenation, append,
comparison, length/charAt/c_str/isEmpty/indexOf/startsWith/endsWith and
read-only indexing) through the CppicString runtime.
.PP
Modes:
.TP
.BR \-\-lex
print the token stream.
.TP
.BR \-\-dump
print the parsed AST.
.TP
.BR \-\-emit
transpile to C (default for .cpp files with setup/loop).
.TP
.BR \-I " dir"
add a directory to the #include search path.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate C from an Arduino-style sketch:
.PP
.nf
    cppic --emit sketch.cpp > sketch.c
.fi
.PP
Link several files (headers are resolved via #include):
.PP
.nf
    cppic --emit main.cpp led.cpp > program.c
.fi
.PP
Build a PIC18 Intel HEX image (requires the sdcc package):
.PP
.nf
    sdcc -mpic18 -p18f87k22 -I/usr/share/cppic/runtime \\
         sketch.c /usr/share/cppic/runtime/cppic_runtime.c
.fi
.PP
Test the sketch on the desktop simulator:
.PP
.nf
    cc -DCPPIC_HOST_SIM -I/usr/share/cppic/runtime \\
       -o sketch sketch.c /usr/share/cppic/runtime/cppic_runtime.c
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/cppic/runtime/cppic_runtime.h
runtime header included by generated code (also provides the small
heaps implementing new/delete and the CppicString type).
.TP
.I /usr/share/cppic/runtime/cppic_runtime.c
runtime implementation (heap + host simulator).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on lex/parse/transpile errors, 2 on usage errors.
